{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And all the house of Israel wept for Aaron thirty days.</b> The men and the women. But in the case of Moses it does not say 'house,' but rather (Deuteronomy 34:8): ״ויבכו בני ישראל את משה בערבות מואב שלשים יום״ — 'And the children of Israel wept for Moses in the plains of Moab thirty days' — because Aaron was a lover of peace and a pursuer of peace, and one who established peace between a person and his fellow and between a man and his wife."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:22.906176486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}